# ─── Help: Getting started ───
help.start.title = Getting started
help.start.step1_title = 1. Install the Android app
help.start.step1_body = Grab the DroidLens app from the GitHub releases page and install it on your phone.
help.start.download_app = Download Android app
help.start.step2_title = 2. Open the app on your phone
help.start.step2_body = Keep DroidLens open on your phone in the foreground. You'll see your IP address and a badge at the top.
help.start.step3_title = 3. Connect over USB or Wi-Fi
help.start.step3_body = DroidLens finds your phone automatically and lists it below. Pick a device and press Start stream — streaming starts only after you press it, not automatically. Both USB and Wi-Fi work the same way.
help.start.connection_hint = The badge next to the device shows how it's connected — USB icon for USB, Wi-Fi icon for Wi-Fi. No device showing up? For USB make sure debugging is enabled (see below); for Wi-Fi make sure both devices are on the same network.
help.start.lock_hint = Heads up: locking your phone's screen interrupts the connection. DroidLens keeps the screen awake automatically while a stream is active, so this shouldn't happen on its own — just don't lock it manually mid-stream.
help.start.usb_debug_title = How to enable USB debugging
help.start.usb_debug_intro = Needed only for USB. For Wi-Fi you can skip this.
help.start.usb_debug_step1 = On your phone open Settings → About phone → tap Build number 7 times until you see “You are now a developer”.
help.start.usb_debug_step2 = Go back to Settings → System → Developer options (on some phones: Settings → Developer options) → enable USB debugging.
help.start.usb_debug_step3 = Connect the phone via USB, allow the “Allow USB debugging?” prompt on the phone (tick “Always allow from this computer”).
help.start.usb_debug_hint2 = If the device does not appear, check the cable integrity or try turning USB debugging off and on again on the device.
help.start.badge_hint = Indigo badge with your IP means waiting. It turns green with a link icon once this PC connects — USB shows the same green badge with “USB connected”.
help.start.autoconnect_hint = Auto-connect (↻) remembers this device and connects automatically next time it appears. You can toggle it on the connected device row.

# ─── Help: Stream settings ───
help.settings.title = Stream settings
help.settings.body = Quality and codec can be changed **anytime**, even mid-stream.
help.settings.resolution_label = Resolution can only be changed **before** you start streaming.\nIt's locked once a stream is active.
help.settings.start_button_hint = The start button turns **yellow** once a stream is active,\nand doubles as the stop button.
help.settings.resolution_hint = Virtual camera lets other apps (Zoom, OBS, Discord) use your phone as a **regular webcam**.

# ─── Help: Live controls ───
help.controls.title = Live controls
help.controls.body = These four buttons send commands straight to your phone, so they work even while it's out of reach.
help.controls.active_hint = The amber highlight means the feature is active — here flashlight is on. Tap again to turn it off.
help.controls.flip = Flip camera — switches between the front and back lens.
help.controls.rotate = Rotate — only available in landscape (regular or reversed).
help.controls.preview = Hide preview — turns off the phone's own screen while streaming, to save battery.
help.controls.flashlight = Flashlight — brightens the screen on the front camera, or turns on the flash on the back camera.

# ─── Help: Video quality ───
help.quality.title = Video quality
help.quality.body = Pick the balance between sharpness, smoothness and CPU usage. Quality and codec can be changed mid-stream — resolution only before you start.
help.quality.codec_title = Codec
help.quality.codec_list = - `H.264` — best compatibility. Works everywhere, lowest CPU on the PC.\n- `H.265` — sharper at the same bitrate, but needs more CPU to decode.\n- `MJPEG` — fallback when hardware encoders are busy. Bigger traffic, no inter-frame compression.
help.quality.quality_title = Quality
help.quality.quality_list = - Low — less traffic, softer picture. Good for slow Wi-Fi.\n- Medium — balanced. Recommended for most phones.\n- High — maximum detail. Needs stable Wi-Fi or USB.
help.quality.resolution_title = Resolution
help.quality.resolution_list = - SD · ≈4:3 — 640×480 — near-square, lightest on Wi-Fi/CPU.\n- HD · 16:9 — 1280×720 — balanced, default.\n- Full HD · 16:9 — 1920×1080 — sharpest, needs stable Wi-Fi or USB.
help.quality.variability_title = Actual FPS & resolution may vary
help.quality.variability_body = The phone's camera controls the real frame rate. In low light, on older phones or when the device is hot, it may drop FPS or lower resolution automatically — this is not a bug. What you see in the preview is what the phone actually sends.

# ─── Help: Preview & capture ───
help.preview.title = Preview & capture
help.preview.body = The preview on your PC is just a viewer — pausing it never stops the stream or the virtual camera.
help.preview.screenshot_title = Screenshot
help.preview.screenshot_body = Hover over the preview to reveal the bottom capsule and click the highlighted camera button. Saves a PNG to `Pictures\DroidLens` — change the folder in Settings → Screenshot save location. Flash animation confirms the capture. Disabled while preview is paused.
help.preview.paused_title = Preview paused
help.preview.paused_body = Pauses rendering on this PC only — the phone keeps streaming and VCam keeps sending video. The preview freezes on the last frame and shows a centered amber banner. Click the same button again to resume.
help.preview.footnote = Don't confuse with Black screen (Eye button in Live controls) — that turns off the phone's own screen to save battery, not the PC preview.
help.preview.metrics_title = Metrics under the preview
help.preview.metrics_body = FPS — preview render rate (½ badge when Limit preview FPS is on). RTT — round-trip to phone in ms. Decode — time to decode one frame (— for MJPEG). Resolution — current stream size (e.g. 1280×720).

# ─── Help: Virtual camera ───
help.vcam.title = Virtual camera
help.vcam.body = Exposes your phone as a regular webcam so Zoom, OBS, Discord, Chrome and any other app can use it.
help.vcam.how_title = How to select it
help.vcam.how_body = When an app asks for a camera, choose `DirectShow Softcam`. If you don't see it, restart the app after starting the stream.
help.vcam.win11_hint = Requires Windows 11 — the DirectShow filter doesn't register on Windows 10.
help.vcam.state_title = States (switch)
help.vcam.state_off = Off — virtual camera disabled.
help.vcam.state_indigo = On (indigo) — VCam active, no stream yet. Ready for apps to connect.
help.vcam.state_amber = On (amber) — VCam active and streaming. Apps receive live video.
help.vcam.tip = Tip: some apps cache the camera list. If Softcam doesn't appear, close and reopen the camera picker.

# ─── Help: Compact mode ───
help.tray.title = Compact mode
help.tray.body = Minimize the window and DroidLens shrinks to a small floating card with the same live controls and a stop button, so you can keep an eye on the stream without the full window open.
help.tray.minimize_hint = The ▼ button in the title bar (next to Minimize/Close) sends DroidLens to tray — stream and VCam keep running. Click the tray icon to open this card or use the tray menu to restore the window.
help.tray.side_live = LIVE/IDLE — stream status. ↗ expands to full window.
help.tray.side_vcam = VCam — amber when live, indigo when idle.
help.tray.side_commands = 4 quick commands — in sync with the sidebar.
help.tray.side_stream = Start/Stop — same as sidebar, disabled without a device.

